      {
        "id": "323",
        "text": "01 / Explain the raw structural hardware architecture?",
        "type": "text",
        "customized": false
      },
      {
        "id": "324",
        "text": "Every handle load node is reinforced with solid, custom-milled high-density raw brass or tempered carbon alloy bars. These elements bypass standard rivet layouts, ensuring permanent geometric integrity.",
        "type": "text",
        "customized": false
      },
      {
        "id": "325",
        "text": "02 / What is the processing blueprint behind the leather weight?",
        "type": "text",
        "customized": false
      },
      {
        "id": "326",
        "text": "We preserve the organic high-density thickness of natural selection full-grain hides. No surface mechanical sanding, buffing, or heavy synthetic coating takes place. The raw texture and natural variations are intentional features.",
        "type": "text",
        "customized": false
      },
      {
        "id": "327",
        "text": "03 / How do custom allocation queuing pipelines run?",
        "type": "text",
        "customized": false
      },
      {
        "id": "328",
        "text": "Production is limited strictly to synchronized micro-batches to eliminate industrial waste pipelines. Once a batch matrix hits maximum capacity limits, production loops cycle offline for roughly 45 to 60 days.",
        "type": "text",
        "customized": false
      },
